## 📚 Standard Library Methods in Java

Java provides many built-in methods in standard classes like `Math`, `System`, etc.

| Method         | Class           | Description                              |
|----------------|------------------|------------------------------------------|
| `print()`      | `System.out`     | Prints to the console.                   |
| `sqrt(x)`      | `Math`           | Returns square root of `x`.              |
| `floor(x)`     | `Math`           | Rounds down to the nearest whole number. |

### 🔹 Example: Using Standard Library Method

```java
public class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    System.out.println("Square root of 16 is: " + Math.sqrt(16));
  }
}
```

---

## 🛠 Summary

- Methods allow modular, reusable, clean coding.
- Defined with `access_modifier return_type methodName(params)`.
- Called using `object.methodName(arguments)`.
- Can be user-defined or standard (built-in).
- Encourage better code design in object-oriented programming.

